<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Understand llmdoc's dual-repository knowledge model, install it for your coding agent, and use the CLI and explicit workflows safely."
  section="overview"
>
  <h1>Detached knowledge, operated deliberately.</h1>
  <p class="lead">llmdoc is a detached engineering knowledge base: an independent Git repository for facts that source code cannot cheaply reconstruct—architecture, constraints, rationale, contracts, failure semantics, and risky workflows. The source repository stays read-only.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Start with retrieval, not a reading marathon.</strong> Pick the one CLI entry point that matches your intent, then stop when you have enough context.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose a route</h2>
  <div class="doc-cards">
    <a href="/docs/getting-started/"><span>01</span><strong>Getting started</strong><small>Create or bind an independent knowledge repository.</small></a>
    <a href="/docs/concepts/"><span>02</span><strong>Core concepts</strong><small>Dual repository, double revision, tri-state, and source.paths.</small></a>
    <a href="/docs/workflows/"><span>03</span><strong>Workflows</strong><small>Retrieve daily; initialize, update, prune, and migrate explicitly.</small></a>
    <a href="/docs/cli/"><span>04</span><strong>CLI reference</strong><small>Binding, retrieval, diagnostics, and semantic commit.</small></a>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

